    "finalText": "Done. The implementation is complete and verified:\n\n- **Stack**: NestJS 11 + TypeORM + `pg` against Postgres via `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded credentials), one migration creating `links` (code unique index, clicks counter).\n- **Endpoints**: `POST /links` (201/409/422), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + atomic `clicks = clicks + 1`, verified 25 concurrent requests → exactly 25), `GET /links` (ascending by id, `{items,total}`) — all error bodies carry an `error` field, malformed JSON is converted to 422 by a custom body-parser middleware.\n- **`start.sh`** compiles, applies pending migrations (idempotent), then `exec node dist/main.js` on `0.0.0.0:8000` foreground — no installs inside.\n- **Verified**: 46/46 assertions in my test suite passed, plus a full stop/restart cycle proving data and click counts persist; README documents `sh start.sh`.\n\nThe DB is left empty, migrations recorded, and port 8000 is free for the automated suite."
